Apple's display suppliers are preparing to begin mass production of OLED panels for the upcoming iPhone Air 2 and iPhone 18, according to a report from Korea's <em><a href="https://en.etnews.com/20261118200001">ETNews</a></em>.<br/>
<br/>
<img src="https://images.macrumors.com/article-new/2025/09/iphone-17-ceramic-shield.jpg" alt="" width="1950" height="1097" class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-1018134" /><br/>
The devices will mark Apple's first spring releases next year as part of the company's new split-launch strategy for its flagship smartphones. Apple already debuted the iPhone 18 Pro models and iPhone Duo in September. The iPhone 18e, Apple's more affordable option, is also expected to launch in the spring.<br/>
<br/>
The report claims Samsung Display and LG Display appear to be aligning their production plans for an expected March 2027 launch schedule. The two companies are expected to start mass production in late December and early January, with Samsung said to be the sole supplier for the iPhone Air 2. Apple is also said to have existing OLED panel inventory that it can use for the Air 2.<br/>
<br/>
Apple will reportedly continue to prioritize production of iPhone 18 Pro and iPhone Duo models through the end of the year, with the latter device already seeing <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/11/16/iphone-duo-orders-early-arrival/">improved shipment times</a> edge into December from the original January 2027 forecast. <br/>
<br/>
The standard iPhone and Air models typically account for more than 30% of total iPhone lineup sales, with the standard model outselling the Air, according to the report.<br/>
<br/>
As for upgrades, the iPhone 18 is rumored to get an A20 chip built on Apple's 2nm process, either 9GB or 12GB of RAM depending on the rumor source, a smaller Dynamic Island, and Apple's C2 modem. <br/>
<br/>
The iPhone Air 2 is expected to gain a second rear camera, with an Ultra Wide lens in addition to the Wide lens. Apple is also likely to increase the battery life of the ultra-slim device, reduce the size of the Dynamic Island, and adopt Apple's 2nm A20 chip for speed and efficiency improvements. The Air 2 is also likely to get the C2 modem.<br/>
